renders a styleable DOM node"},"3290":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"button, select-trigger, dialog-popup"},"3291":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"No passthrough"},"3292":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"Interactive parts must be wrapped; never const X = Base.Trigger"},"3293":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"DialogTrigger (good), PopoverTrigger (gap)"},"3294":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"Exempt"},"3295":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"Parts with no styleable DOM output"},"3296":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"Provider, state-only Root, bare Portal"},"3297":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"@base-ui/react and cmdk do not ship data-slot. Direct re-exports have no slot until Vital Design adds a forwardRef wrapper. Do not expect slots on Select root or ToastPortal — scope via child parts such as select-trigger or toast-content instead."},"3298":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Last updated: 2026-07-03. Applies to src-v2/components/ (43 folders)."},"3299":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Status"},"3300":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Components"},"3301":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Full"},"3302":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"alert, avatar, badge, breadcrumb, button, button-group, card, checkbox, chip, collapsible, combobox (incl. tags value), command, dropdown-menu, editable, field, input, number-input, item, label, password-input, popover, progress, radio-group, resizable, scroll-area, search-bar, separator, skeleton, slider, spinner, split-button, switch, table, table-of-contents, tabs, tag, textarea, time-picker, toolbar"},"3303":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Near-full (root/portal passthrough only)"},"3304":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"select, dialog, sheet, tooltip, toast, input-group, autocomplete"},"3305":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Partial"},"3306":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"calendar (month/year dropdown triggers in caption)"},"3307":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Tier 3 exemptions (no slot by design): Provider, state-only Root, bare Portal on select, dialog, dropdown-menu, popover, tooltip, toast, and autocomplete. AutocompleteValue / ComboboxValue also exempt — they render no DOM (text/children only)."},"3308":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"page","content":"Colors","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors"},"3309":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-0","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","content":"Vital Design color system — primitive palettes, semantic aliases, and named component tokens."},"3310":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-1","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Overview"},"3311":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-2","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#primary","content":"Primary"},"3312":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-3","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale","content":"Grayscale"},"3313":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-4","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale-opacity","content":"Grayscale (Opacity)"},"3314":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-5","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#success","content":"Success"},"3315":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-6","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#info","content":"Info"},"3316":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-7","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#warning","content":"Warning"},"3317":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-8","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#destructive","content":"Destructive"},"3318":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-9","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#semantic-tokens","content":"Semantic Tokens"},"3319":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-10","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#surfaces","content":"Surfaces"},"3320":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-11","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Actions"},"3321":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-12","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Status"},"3322":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-13","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Form"},"3323":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-14","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Charts"},"3324":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-15","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Sidebar"},"3325":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-16","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#vital-extensions","content":"Vital Extensions"},"3326":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-17","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#avatar-palette","content":"Avatar Palette"},"3327":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-18","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#tag-palette","content":"Tag Palette"},"3328":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-19","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Vital Design follows the shadcn/ui\nnaming convention for its semantic layer. Colors are defined under\ntokens/ (Style Dictionary), built into src-v2/styles/tokens/generated.css\nas CSS custom properties on :root, and exposed to Tailwind via\n@theme inline (--color-*)."},"3329":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-20","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Primitive scales (--primary-50…900, --grayscale-100…900,\n--grayscale-opacity-100…900, --success-100…900, etc.) — internal\nfoundation. Reach for these when you need a specific shade for\ncharts, illustrations, or fine-grained tinting. Tailwind utility:\nbg-primary-500, text-grayscale-700, etc."},"3330":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-21","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Semantic tokens (--background, --primary, --card,\n--destructive, …) — the public API. These describe intent\nand pair with -foreground siblings for legible content on the\nsurface. Tailwind utility: bg-primary text-primary-foreground."},"3331":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-22","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Component tokens (--avatar-*-fg, --tag-*-solid) — closed\npalettes used by specific components."},"3332":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-23","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#primary","content":"The primary palette is a blue scale used for interactive elements,\nbuttons, focus states, and key affordances."},"3333":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-24","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale","content":"The default grayscale palette is fully solid — use it whenever the\nsurface must be opaque (popovers, tooltips, toasts, solid chips)."},"3334":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-25","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale-opacity","content":"The opacity variant uses rgba(35, 35, 50, α) so it tonally adapts\nover any background. Use it for hover tints, dividers, disabled fields,\nand other states where translucency is desired. --grayscale-opacity-900\nis the only solid hex."},"3335":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-26","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#success","content":"Positive feedback, confirmations, \"saved\" states."},"3336":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-27","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#info","content":"Informational messaging and neutral status indicators."},"3337":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-28","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#warning","content":"Caution states — soft warnings that don't block flow."},"3338":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-29","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#destructive","content":"Errors, destructive actions, hard validation failures."},"3339":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-30","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#semantic-tokens","content":"Intent-based aliases that point to primitive colors. Each surface\nships with a paired -foreground token — use them together so text\nremains legible regardless of theme overrides."},"3340":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-31","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#surfaces","content":"Page chrome, cards, popovers, and muted/accent regions. background\nis the page; card and popover are elevated containers; muted\nand accent are subtle background tints (e.g. table stripes, hover\nstates)."},"3341":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-32","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Brand action surfaces. primary is the dominant call-to-action;\nsecondary is the alternative button surface."},"3342":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-33","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Feedback colors paired with foreground for legible content."},"3343":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-34","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Borders, input strokes, and focus rings. border is the canonical\nsolid divider; input matches it by default but can be themed\nindependently; ring paints focus outlines."},"3344":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-35","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Five-step palette for data visualization. Defaults rotate through\nprimary → success → warning → info → destructive so char